cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FinCom Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "FinCom Bench"
abstract: >-
  A public benchmark for financial compliance and behaviour in AI chat replies.
  FinCom Bench sends probes to an AI assistant and grades the replies against
  real conduct rules from four jurisdictions: the United Kingdom, the European
  Union, the United States and Australia. It scores two axes — compliance
  (did the content break a named rule?) and behaviour (did the assistant use a
  manipulative or a helpful technique?) — across 15 finding categories. The
  headline output is a leaderboard of AI assistants. The repository holds the
  rule records with their citations, the probe datasets, the grading harness,
  and the run transcript behind every leaderboard row.
type: software
authors:
